    "**Observations**\n",
    "\n",
    "- All 17 sensor files have exactly 2,205 cycles and **no missing values**, so no imputation is needed.\n",
    "- File widths match the sampling rates over a 60 s cycle: 100 Hz → 6,000 values, 10 Hz → 600, 1 Hz → 60.\n",
    "- The **cooler** condition is almost perfectly balanced (732 / 732 / 741 cycles). The other components are not: the valve is optimal in 1,125 cycles (vs 360 for each fault level), the pump has no leakage in 1,221, and the accumulator sits at 90 bar in 808.\n",
    "- About two thirds of cycles (1,449) are flagged as stable. Unstable cycles are kept: the goal is to profile all operating states, not only steady ones."
   ]
