    "**Observations**\n",
    "\n",
    "- PS1 moves through **flat pressure plateaus** (about 146–191 bar) that change every 10 s. This is the test rig's programmed load cycle, and it repeats every cycle.\n",
    "- FS1 is near zero for the first ~9 s, then holds around 8 l/min, with short spikes at each load switch.\n",
    "- TS1 changes by less than 1 °C within a cycle; temperature varies far more *between* cycles than within one.\n",
    "- Because each cycle is mostly steady plateaus, mean, std, min and max capture its level and spread well. What they lose is the **timing and shape of the switching transients** — a limitation that matters later for the valve."
   ]
  },
