   "source": [
    "print(\"Missing values:     \", int(X.isna().sum().sum()))\n",
    "print(\"Duplicate cycles:   \", int(X.duplicated().sum()))\n",
    "constant_cols = list(X.columns[X.std() == 0])\n",
    "print(\"Constant features:  \", constant_cols)\n",
    "\n",
    "# A feature with the same value in every cycle carries no information for clustering\n",
    "X = X.drop(columns=constant_cols)\n",
    "print(\"Features after dropping constants:\", X.shape[1])\n",
    "\n",
    "# Outlier count per feature (1.5 x IQR rule), for information\n",
    "q1, q3 = X.quantile(0.25), X.quantile(0.75)\n",
    "iqr = q3 - q1\n",
    "outliers = ((X < q1 - 1.5 * iqr) | (X > q3 + 1.5 * iqr)).sum()\n",
    "print(\"Cycles flagged as outliers in at least one feature:\",\n",
    "      int(((X < q1 - 1.5 * iqr) | (X > q3 + 1.5 * iqr)).any(axis=1).sum()))\n",
    "outliers.sort_values(ascending=False).head(10).to_frame(\"outlier_cycles\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "056b0222",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Observations**\n",
    "\n",
    "- `PS2_min`, `PS3_min` and `SE_min` are **0 in every cycle**: these sensors drop to zero at some point in every load cycle, so their minimum says nothing about the cycle. They were dropped, leaving 65 features.\n",
    "- No missing values and no duplicate cycles.\n",
    "- The 1.5 × IQR rule flags **1,374 of 2,205 cycles (62%)** in at least one feature. That is far too many to be measurement errors; it happens because the features are multi-modal (previous section), so whole operating states fall outside one IQR range. For example, the 240 PS1_mean outliers are exactly one of the clusters found later.\n",
    "- **Decision: outliers are kept.** In condition monitoring the extreme cycles are the degraded states the clustering is meant to find; removing them would delete the signal."
   ]
  },
