   "source": [
    "**Observations**\n",
    "\n",
    "- **The clusters follow the cooler condition** (ARI ≈ 0.85). The other components barely line up (ARI < 0.08 for valve, pump and accumulator).\n",
    "- In plain words:\n",
    "  - **Full-efficiency cooler (healthy):** 100% of its cycles have the cooler at 100%.\n",
    "  - **Reduced-efficiency cooler:** 96% at 20% cooler efficiency.\n",
    "  - **Cooler close to failure:** 99% at 3% cooler; the other components are mostly healthy (78% no pump leakage, 64% accumulator at its optimal 130 bar).\n",
    "  - **Critical — cooler close to failure with pump leakage:** all 240 cycles have the cooler at 3%, 94% have pump leakage, and 98% have a reduced accumulator pressure. This is a **multi-fault state**, and it is the group that stood out in the EDA and in PCA (low flow, low efficiency factor, unsteady pressure).\n",
    "- **The valve condition is not recovered:** each valve level appears in roughly the same share of every cluster. Valve lag shows up in the timing of switching transients, which the summary statistics smooth out (see Section 3).\n",
    "- Clustering without labels therefore rediscovers real, physically meaningful machine health states — mainly the cooler, plus one combined-fault state."
   ]
  },
